{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/control-reader-brief.md /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-3.json'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/control-reader-brief.md /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-3.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 9,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a guarantee of OpenAI's Ohio data-center lease by 2027-06-30?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-06-30\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by the due day.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"It has not.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA sign a financial guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease by 2027-07-01?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA guarantee for OpenAI’s Ohio data-center lease\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-07-01\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not signed the guarantee by 2027-07-01.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has signed the guarantee by 2027-07-01.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i005\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (per The Information)\",\n     \"what\": \"negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of a large Ohio data center\",\n     \"how_much\": \"the data center could cost as much as $500 billion if fully built (asset cost, not the guarantee amount)\",\n     \"condition\": \"in negotiation; nothing signed\",\n     \"status\": \"rumour\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i006\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"guarantees of customer data center leases, in exchange for rights to buy their shares\",\n     \"how_much\": \"an additional $3.5 billion\",\n     \"period\": \"quarter ended April 2026 (filed May)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i116\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia is diving even deeper, as it has started backstopping datacenter leases\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA backstops datacenter leases for neoclouds (a second kind of obligation)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i119\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e8 [rumour; moomoo.com, citing The Information; original source The Information ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] The Information previously reported that NVIDIA was negotiating to guarantee OpenAI’s lease of a large Ohio data center, whose fully built-out cost could reach $500 billion.\\n    Quote: According to prior reporting by The Information, NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio—an asset that, if fully built out at current prices for chips, labor, power, and other materials, could cost as much as $500 billion.\",\n   \"- e15 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Nvidia announced a partnership program using AI cloud providers to give AI startups access to computing infrastructure.\\n    Quote: Chipmaker Nvidia is expanding its support for fast-growing AI startups by introducing a partnership program that leverages its network of AI cloud service providers to offer these firms access to critical computing infrastructure, the company said Thursday.\",\n   \"- e16 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Under Nvidia’s announced partnership program, cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share product and cloud revenue with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share both product and cloud revenue with Nvidia, which is positioning itself as an intermediary helping startups gain direct access to full-stack computing powered by Nvidia chips.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e10, e24, e25; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e17 [fact; CNBC; original source Sharon AI 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs through the program.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e23; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e18 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Firmus Technologies 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, expected to reach 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\",\n   \"- e19 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA is acting as a financial backstop for AI-cloud customers in exchange for a share of their revenue.\\n    Quote: The chip designer is acting as a financial backstop for companies in exchange for a share in their revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e20 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Under the backstop, NVIDIA agrees to rent back unused GPUs from AI-cloud customers at a fixed rate.\\n    Quote: The backstop sees Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate.\",\n   \"- e21 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source Firmus and Sharon AI ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Firmus and Sharon AI are among the first companies to adopt NVIDIA's AI-cloud backstop offer.\\n    Quote: Firmus and Sharon AI are among the first companies to have adopted the offer.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e22 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia.\\n    Quote: Firmus is deploying 170,000 GPUs in Batam, Indonesia,\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e13; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e23 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI is deploying 40,000 GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e17, e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e24 [party_statement; NVIDIA, in a post quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA said its new model lets AI clouds procure NVIDIA infrastructure through a revenue-sharing and credit-support model serving AI-native, enterprise, and ISV customers.\\n    Quote: This new model enables AI clouds to procure Nvidia infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise, and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e16; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e25 [party_statement; NVIDIA, in a post quoted by datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA said the partnerships will generate product revenue plus a share of cloud revenue on supported capacity, creating a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\\n    Quote: Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell Nvidia-powered cloud services, with Nvidia earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates adoption of Nvidia platforms among the high-growth, high-conviction AI native sector, and provides Nvidia with a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e16, e26; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e19 [fact; datacenterdynamics.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:c3e020d179ab025bf3ba56b0 2026-07-02] NVIDIA is acting as a financial backstop for AI-cloud customers in exchange for a share of their revenue.\\n    Quote: The chip designer is acting as a financial backstop for companies in exchange for a share in their revenue.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1, e61; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e178 [party_statement; Futuriom, quoting NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress and VP of Global AI Clouds and Infrastructure Ecosystem Raj Mirpuri said the new AI-cloud partnership model combines credit support and revenue sharing, with NVIDIA earning product revenue and a share of cloud revenue on supported capacity.\\n    Quote: “This new model enables AI clouds to procure NVIDIA infrastructure for AI-native, enterprise and ISV customers through economic alignment with a revenue-sharing and credit-support model. Through the partnership, AI clouds will sell NVIDIA-powered cloud services, with NVIDIA earning both standard product revenue and a share of the cloud revenue on the supported capacity. This structure accelerates \\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e44; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e179 [party_statement; Futuriom; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] NVIDIA said Sharon AI signed onto its AI-cloud plan and will buy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA states that two AI cloud providers have already signed on for the new deal: Sharon AI, based in Australia, will buy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under the plan.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e37; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e180 [fact; Futuriom; original source Firmus ; from gnews:cb05b9f49943ef0ba412cf36 2026-07-08] Firmus is building a DSX AI factory in Indonesia expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus, based in Indoesia, is building a DSX AI factory there that’s expected to scale to 360 megawatts and contain up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e38; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e451 [fact; Jakarta Globe; original source Firmus Technologies and DayOne ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Firmus Technologies and DayOne are developing NVIDIA's DSX AI Factory Campus in Batam, a planned 360 MW AI data-center complex.\\n    Quote: The Batam development marks Firmus Technologies' first data center investment in Indonesia. The Australian AI infrastructure company is partnering with Singapore-based data center operator DayOne to develop the Nvidia DSX AI Factory Campus, a 360-megawatt AI data center complex that is expected to become one of Southeast Asia's largest AI computing hubs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e46; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e452 [third_party_view; Jakarta Globe, citing The Straits Times; original source The Straits Times ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] The Straits Times projected that the Batam campus could generate up to $30 billion in off-take agreements during its first six years of operation.\\n    Quote: According to The Straits Times , the project is projected to generate as much as $30 billion in off-take agreements during its first six years of operation.\",\n   \"- e453 [party_statement; Jakarta Globe; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:e001119c6342373f6b1f3cf4 2026-07-14] Firmus plans to deploy about 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs in phases from Q1 2027 through early 2028 to provide AI computing capacity for startups and fast-growing AI companies.\\n    Quote: Under the partnership, Firmus plans to deploy about 170,000 of Nvidia's latest-generation graphics processing units (GPUs) in phases from the first quarter of 2027 through early 2028, providing AI computing capacity for startups and fast-growing AI companies.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e99; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 10,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"yes/no\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Nvidia has not begun shipping Rubin by December 31, 2026.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v3\",\n   \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Rubin-generation platform by the end of 2026.\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Yes\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA begins shipping Rubin on or before 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"No\",\n    \"condition\": \"NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i105\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-05\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin systems in full production; shipping to eight cloud partners including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall (2026)\",\n     \"status\": \"happened (full production); plan (shipping this fall)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i219\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\",\n    \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\",\n     \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"plan\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i202\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\",\n     \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\",\n     \"period\": \"2026\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i207\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\",\n    \"passage\": \"the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (as restated)\",\n     \"what\": \"Rubin systems in full production; first shipments to eight cloud partners incl. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud\",\n     \"period\": \"this fall\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"in full production; shipping this fall is a plan\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e29 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source fool.com 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The article says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is in full production and could begin shipping in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\",\n   \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\",\n   \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e34 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast $1 trillion in combined Blackwell and Vera Rubin chip sales from March through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e30; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e39 [fact; BGR.com, reporting on NVIDIA's blog post by Josh Parker; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA announced that its DSX AI factories are hosting Rubin AI infrastructure, using a design with no fans or cold aisles.\\n    Quote: In Nvidia's blog post by Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at Nvidia, it was announced that Nvidia DSX AI factories are hosting Nvidia's Rubin AI infrastructure with no fans or cold aisles.\",\n   \"- e47 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra, had been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\",\n   \"- e48 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis’s report and said its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\",\n   \"- e49 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture was delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remained difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\",\n   \"- e50 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks, was likely to be delayed or produced in only small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\",\n   \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\",\n   \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\",\n   \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\",\n   \"- e55 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\",\n   \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e125; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e119, e120; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e129; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e76 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source MarketScale 2026-07-06; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] First shipments of the Vera Rubin VR200 are scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\",\n   \"- e79 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis had reported that NVIDIA canceled its four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design, citing manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: The news comes a week after SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of the two-chiplet design, also due to “manufacturing execution concerns.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e90 [rumour; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Unnamed reports cited by 247wallst.com ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\",\n   \"- e116 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA had canceled the four-compute-die version of its upcoming Rubin Ultra chip.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e79, e126; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e117 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said only the two-die Rubin Ultra version remained, with roughly half the real-world compute performance of the canceled four-die version.\\n    Quote: Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\",\n   \"- e118 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology would not arrive until the Feynman generation, the generation after next.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\",\n   \"- e119 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA currently lacked a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems.\\n    Quote: That means Nvidia lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e120 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said the gap in NVIDIA's ability to scale Rubin Ultra could give AMD's MI500X and Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to compete.\\n    Quote: The gap could give competitors like AMD's MI500X or Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to move in.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e121 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA planned to offset the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\",\n   \"- e125 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis alleged that NVIDIA cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design after operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Quote: The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e51; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e126 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed NVIDIA scrapped a four-die configuration of its upcoming Rubin Ultra platform in favor of a downsized version.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e129 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source tikr.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: That’s likely because the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e278 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author said the $300 NVIDIA share-price case depended on Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin shipping on schedule, gross margins remaining at 75%, and a sovereign or hyperscaler deal being upsized.\\n    Quote: Three things need to go right: Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin ship on schedule, gross margins hold the 75% line, and one sovereign or hyperscaler deal gets upsized in a headline print.\",\n   \"- e350 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\",\n   \"- e351 [fact; en.sedaily.com; original source LG Electronics ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in the first half of 2026 and plans to seek orders after second-half reliability evaluations, with mass production planned for 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\",\n   \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\",\n   \"- e427 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Blackwell 300 was ramping, with the Vera Rubin platform queued behind it.\\n    Quote: Blackwell 300 is ramping, and the Vera Rubin platform is queued behind it.\",\n   \"- e445 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for late-2026 delivery, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 11,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $550 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $550 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 550000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$550 billion to below $600 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $550 billion and less than $600 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 550000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 600000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$600 billion to below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $600 billion and less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 600000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less t