organ Stanley\",\n     \"what\": \"revenue growth rates accelerating\",\n     \"how_much\": \"quarterly revenue approaching $100 bn\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e40 [fact; fool.com; original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan around $650 billion of data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\",\n   \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e111 [third_party_view; Allen Harris; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated that annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026\",\n   \"- e122 [third_party_view; the-decoder.com; original source Gary Tan of Allspring Global Investments ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] Gary Tan of Allspring Global Investments said the reported Kyber delay did not necessarily mean overall AI spending would shrink.\\n    Quote: A Kyber delay doesn't necessarily mean overall AI spending will shrink, said Gary Tan of Allspring Global Investments, according to Bloomberg .\",\n   \"- e40 [fact; fool.com; original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan around $650 billion of data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e148, e152; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e148 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author estimates that the four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e161 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reports analysts expect NVIDIA’s share within Meta to decline while major cloud providers’ overall AI capital expenditures rise significantly.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40, e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e386 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital-expenditure forecast to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute to rent excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reports analysts expect NVIDIA’s share within Meta to decline while major cloud providers’ overall AI capital expenditures rise significantly.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e398; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e398 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Meta, Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Meta, Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon are planning higher capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers, including Meta Platforms , Microsoft , Alphabet , and Amazon , are planning higher capital expenditures in 2026.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e280; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e412 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com (Vandita Jadeja); original source Meta ; from gnews:1e1fa5a194198eaf05d90c9e 2026-07-14] Meta has a $145 billion infrastructure budget aimed partly at custom silicon, which could bear on demand for NVIDIA chips.\\n    Quote: Meta’s $145B infrastructure budget aimed partly at custom silicon.\"\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"control\": 12,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"How much will the largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Below $700 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 700000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$700 billion to below $800 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $800 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 700000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$800 billion to below $900 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion and less than $900 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$900 billion to below $1000 billion\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion and less than $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 1000000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"$1000 billion or more\",\n     \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1000 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 1000000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v5\",\n   \"question\": \"How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"Calendar 2027 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2028-03-31\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"theme\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Lowest range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is below $800 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 800000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Lower-middle range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $800 billion but below $900 billion.\",\n    \"lo\": 800000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 900000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral comparison: around NVIDIA's reported $1 trillion projection\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $900 billion but below $1.1 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 900000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1100000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Upper-middle range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.1 trillion but below $1.2 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1100000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 1200000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Highest range\",\n    \"condition\": \"Combined spending is at least $1.2 trillion.\",\n    \"lo\": 1200000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i256\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-07\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\",\n    \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\",\n     \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\",\n     \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\",\n     \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\",\n     \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i090\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-04\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Nearly Flat for 2026. Time to Cash Out, or Load Up on Shares?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Wall Street analysts project 82% revenue growth for this year and 41% next year\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Wall Street analysts\",\n     \"what\": \"NVIDIA revenue growth forecast\",\n     \"how_much\": \"82% this year; 41% next year\",\n     \"period\": \"this year and next year (fiscal or calendar both accepted, D233)\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i143\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"How Nvidia Became The Black Sheep Of The Chip Stock Rally\",\n    \"passage\": \"Some estimates put half of all data center spend going toward memory in 2027.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"unnamed estimates\",\n     \"what\": \"memory's share of data center spend\",\n     \"how_much\": \"about half\",\n     \"period\": \"2027\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i161\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"CAPITAL IDEAS: The lag 7 — Is Micron the new Nvidia?\",\n    \"passage\": \"Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026 and grow to $1.6 trillion by 2031\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Goldman Sachs estimate\",\n     \"what\": \"annual AI infrastructure capex (chips, data centers, power, cooling, networking)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$765B (2026); $1.6T (2031); ~$7.6T cumulative 2026-2031\",\n     \"period\": \"2026; 2031; 2026-2031\",\n     \"condition\": \"could reach\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e41 [party_statement; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\",\n   \"- e41 [party_statement; fool.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] NVIDIA projects that the four largest AI hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditures could reach $1 trillion in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia projects that this figure could reach $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e80; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e149 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA says the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e80; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e280 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reports analysts expect NVIDIA’s share within Meta to decline while major cloud providers’ overall AI capital expenditures rise significantly.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\",\n   \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40, e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e315 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] NVIDIA told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to exceed $1 trillion next year.\\n    Quote: Nvidia told investors last quarter that it expects AI hyperaccelerator spending to rise to over $1 trillion next year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e152; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e316 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-12; from gnews:07cf5835d106467db5448c13 2026-07-12] The author estimates that NVIDIA likely already has orders on the books for next year, giving it visibility into demand.\\n    Quote: I'm more inclined to believe Nvidia over the market's skepticism, as it likely has orders on the books for next year, so it can easily see the demand already.\",\n   \"- e149 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] NVIDIA says the four largest AI hyperscalers will spend more than $1 trillion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2027.\\n    Quote: Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e80, e390; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e390 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com, reporting Morgan Stanley’s forecast; original source Morgan Stanley ; from gnews:e0e5ab6c2aced8d5a6a688a5 2026-07-13] Morgan Stanley forecasts that Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta will spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure in calendar 2027 and add 19.5 GW of incremental compute capacity that year.\\n    Quote: The analyst says Google, Amazon, Microsoft, and Meta are forecast to spend over $1 trillion on AI infrastructure next year, adding 19.5 gigawatts (GW) of incremental compute capacity.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\"\n  ]\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-3.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"]),print(\\\"RULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"]),print(\\\"JUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"]),print(\\\"ITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"],ensure_ascii=False)),print(\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"],ensure_ascii=False))) for x in p if x[\\\"control\\\"] in (10,11)]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=json.load(open(\\\"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/full-eligibility/controls/control-packet-3.json\\\")); [(print(\\\"CONTROL\\\",x[\\\"control\\\"]),print(\\\"RULER\\\",x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"question\\\"],x[\\\"ruler_question\\\"][\\\"due_day\\\"]),print(\\\"JUDGED\\\",x[\\\"judged_question\\\"]),print(\\\"ITEMS\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"reader_b_decisive_items\\\"],ensure_ascii=False)),print(\\\"EVIDENCE\\\",json.dumps(x[\\\"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\\\"],ensure_ascii=False))) for x in p if x[\\\"control\\\"] in (10,11)]'\"","aggregated_output":"CONTROL 10\nRULER Will Nvidia begin shipping its Rubin generation by December 31, 2026? 2026-12-31\nJUDGED {'view_id': 'v3', 'question': 'Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin by 2026-12-31?', 'looks_at': 'Whether NVIDIA begins shipping its Rubin-generation platform by the end of 2026.', 'due_day': '2026-12-31', 'year': '2026', 'kind': 'asset'}\nITEMS [{\"id\": \"i105\", \"day\": \"2026-07-05\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's next-gen AI rack system delayed to 2028 on manufacturing snags, SemiAnalysis says\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA\", \"what\": \"Vera Rubin systems in full production; shipping to eight cloud partners including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud\", \"period\": \"this fall (2026)\", \"status\": \"happened (full production); plan (shipping this fall)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i219\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Vera Rubin rack costs $7.8M — memory is why\", \"passage\": \"First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\", \"meaning\": {\"what\": \"Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 first shipments and volume ramp\", \"period\": \"first shipments Q3 2026; volume ramp Q4 2026\", \"status\": \"plan\"}}, {\"id\": \"i202\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia's Kyber rack for Rubin Ultra reportedly delayed to 2028, stopgap solution also axed due to customer pushback — Analyst firm SemiAnalysis says PCB midplane problems led to the delay [Updated]\", \"passage\": \"Nvidia's 2026 Rubin GPUs, which reuse the current Oberon rack, aren't part of the reported delay.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Tom's Hardware\", \"what\": \"scope of the reported delay: Rubin Ultra/Kyber only; 2026 Rubin on Oberon unaffected\", \"period\": \"2026\", \"status\": \"claim\"}}, {\"id\": \"i207\", \"day\": \"2026-07-06\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Delays Next-Generation Kyber Server Architecture as Manufacturing Hurdles Give Rivals a Rare Opening\", \"passage\": \"the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"NVIDIA (as restated)\", \"what\": \"Rubin systems in full production; first shipments to eight cloud partners incl. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud\", \"period\": \"this fall\", \"status\": \"happened\", \"status_note\": \"in full production; shipping this fall is a plan\"}}]\nEVIDENCE [\"- e29 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source fool.com 2026-07-02; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] The article says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is in full production and could begin shipping in 2026.\\n    Quote: Vera Rubin, Nvidia's next-generation AI chip platform, is in full production and could begin shipping later this year.\", \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\", \"- e30 [party_statement; fool.com; original source Jensen Huang ; from gnews:af6e4910e877d5682a773d4b 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang expects $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Quote: CEO Jensen Huang has laid out expectations for $1 trillion in orders for Vera Rubin and Grace Blackwell chips through 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e34 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst), quoting Jensen Huang; original source Jensen Huang, NVIDIA CEO ; from gnews:e4e5f1b5c0c68381e4c486e1 2026-07-03] NVIDIA CEO Jensen Huang forecast $1 trillion in combined Blackwell and Vera Rubin chip sales from March through the end of 2027.\\n    Quote: In March, CEO Jensen Huang said he expects the company's Blackwell and Vera Rubin chips to generate $1 trillion in sales between that time and the end of 2027.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e30; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e39 [fact; BGR.com, reporting on NVIDIA's blog post by Josh Parker; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:a8fab49de53d125314a6688a 2026-07-04] NVIDIA announced that its DSX AI factories are hosting Rubin AI infrastructure, using a design with no fans or cold aisles.\\n    Quote: In Nvidia's blog post by Josh Parker, head of corporate sustainability at Nvidia, it was announced that Nvidia DSX AI factories are hosting Nvidia's Rubin AI infrastructure with no fans or cold aisles.\", \"- e47 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA’s Kyber rack-scale architecture, designed for Rubin Ultra, had been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028.\\n    Quote: Nvidia 's next marquee product — the Kyber rack-scale architecture designed to house its 2027 Rubin Ultra chips — has been delayed by more than 12 months to 2028, according to research firm SemiAnalysis\", \"- e48 [party_statement; CNBC, quoting NVIDIA; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA rejected SemiAnalysis’s report and said its product roadmap remained intact.\\n    Quote: Nvidia rejected the SemiAnalysis report and said, \\\"Our roadmap is intact.\\\"\", \"- e49 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said the Kyber NVL144 rack architecture was delayed to 2028 because its PCB midplane remained difficult to manufacture.\\n    Quote: \\\"Kyber NVL144 rack architecture has been delayed to 2028 as the PCB midplane remains challenging from a manufacturability standpoint,\\\" the firm said\", \"- e50 [rumour; CNBC; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA’s NVL576 system, which links eight racks, was likely to be delayed or produced in only small volumes.\\n    Quote: NVL576 — a larger system linking eight racks via optical connections — is also likely delayed or limited to small volumes, the research firm said.\", \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\", \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\", \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\", \"- e55 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2f953a56cd06571ab0afc348 2026-07-05] NVIDIA plans to launch its first stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\\n    Quote: In fact, it's launching its first-ever stand-alone CPU this fall as part of the Vera Rubin platform.\", \"- e51 [rumour; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA scrapped its backup plan to bolt two current-generation racks together after cloud providers and hyperscalers objected to the design and operating burden.\\n    Quote: A backup plan — bolting two of Nvidia's current-generation racks together for similar power — has also been scrapped after cloud customers rejected the design as awkward and costly to operate. \\\"It has since been cancelled due to heavy pushback from CSPs [cloud service providers] and hyperscalers over its odd design and heavy operational burden,\\\" SemiAnalysis said.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e125; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e52 [third_party_view; CNBC, quoting SemiAnalysis; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA had no proven solution to expand Rubin Ultra’s scale-up system size and that this could give AMD and Google a technical opening in the high-end market.\\n    Quote: That leaves Nvidia with \\\"no proven solution to expand the scale-up world size for Rubin Ultra,\\\" SemiAnalysis said, predicting that could give rivals Advanced Micro Devices and Google , whose in-house chips are already winning business from top AI labs, a rare technical opening at the high end of the market.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e119, e120; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e53 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:552f8c2bdfd080555d592587 2026-07-05] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems were in full production and were scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: Nvidia's current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and begin shipping this fall to eight cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e129; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e76 [third_party_view; MarketScale; original source MarketScale 2026-07-06; from gnews:f66e1689ec2e27e7eab2a2dd 2026-07-06] First shipments of the Vera Rubin VR200 are scheduled for Q3 2026, with volume ramping in Q4.\\n    Quote: First shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth.\", \"- e79 [rumour; datacenterdynamics.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:98a4e8ff0c0260d8dc9e531d 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis had reported that NVIDIA canceled its four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of a two-chiplet design, citing manufacturing execution concerns.\\n    Quote: The news comes a week after SemiAnalysis separately reported that Nvidia had canceled the four-die Rubin Ultra design in favor of the two-chiplet design, also due to “manufacturing execution concerns.”\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e90 [rumour; 247wallst.com (Danielle Liverance); original source Unnamed reports cited by 247wallst.com ; from gnews:3df0bbc8aff2c1d008bc0a32 2026-07-06] Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA shares are under pressure on reports of delays across their upcoming lineup of Vera Rubin server systems.\", \"- e116 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA had canceled the four-compute-die version of its upcoming Rubin Ultra chip.\\n    Quote: The more powerful version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra chip with four compute dies has also been canceled.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e79, e126; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e117 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said only the two-die Rubin Ultra version remained, with roughly half the real-world compute performance of the canceled four-die version.\\n    Quote: Only the smaller two-die version remains, delivering roughly half the real-world compute performance.\", \"- e118 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA's CPO-NVSwitch interconnect technology would not arrive until the Feynman generation, the generation after next.\\n    Quote: A key interconnect technology called CPO-NVSwitch, which links many chips into a single large system, won't arrive until the generation after next, called Feynman.\", \"- e119 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said NVIDIA currently lacked a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems.\\n    Quote: That means Nvidia lacks a proven way to scale Rubin Ultra to very large systems for now.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e120 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis said the gap in NVIDIA's ability to scale Rubin Ultra could give AMD's MI500X and Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to compete.\\n    Quote: The gap could give competitors like AMD's MI500X or Google's TPUv8i Broadfly room to move in.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e52; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e121 [rumour; the-decoder.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis reported that NVIDIA planned to offset the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\\n    Quote: Nvidia plans to make up for the shortfall by selling more Oberon-Rubin racks in the existing form factor.\", \"- e125 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis alleged that NVIDIA cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design after operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Quote: The research firm further alleged that Nvidia cancelled an alternative back-to-back rack design following heavy operational pushback from hyperscale cloud clients.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e51; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e126 [rumour; Investing.com; original source SemiAnalysis ; from gnews:d5c48abb470f394f86549b6b 2026-07-06] SemiAnalysis claimed NVIDIA scrapped a four-die configuration of its upcoming Rubin Ultra platform in favor of a downsized version.\\n    Quote: Additionally, the report pointed to a downsized version of the upcoming Rubin Ultra platform, claiming a crucial four-die configuration had been scrapped.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e116; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e129 [third_party_view; tikr.com (analyst); original source tikr.com (analyst) 2026-07-06; from gnews:d4c5dc540392f8df39aee250 2026-07-06] NVIDIA’s current-generation Rubin systems are in full production and are scheduled to begin shipping in fall 2026 to eight major cloud partners, including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Quote: That’s likely because the company’s current-generation Rubin systems are already in full production and set to start shipping this fall to eight major cloud partners, including Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e53; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e278 [third_party_view; Vandita Jadeja; original source Vandita Jadeja 2026-07-10; from gnews:f0423de52e9bd77b530ba76e 2026-07-10] The author said the $300 NVIDIA share-price case depended on Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin shipping on schedule, gross margins remaining at 75%, and a sovereign or hyperscaler deal being upsized.\\n    Quote: Three things need to go right: Blackwell Ultra and Vera Rubin ship on schedule, gross margins hold the 75% line, and one sovereign or hyperscaler deal gets upsized in a headline print.\", \"- e350 [fact; barchart.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ededac685b09f7a9c6952202 2026-07-12] NVIDIA recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform.\\n    Quote: Nvidia recently launched its Vera Rubin AI platform, released the AI PC platform RTX Spark, expanded partnerships with companies such as Alphabet (GOOGL) and Marvell (MRVL), and further invested in networking, CPUs, and AI infrastructure.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\", \"- e351 [fact; en.sedaily.com; original source LG Electronics ; from gnews:bf96def37a9c3a5f19f5d43c 2026-07-12] LG Electronics completed a Vera Rubin-specification AI server rack prototype in the first half of 2026 and plans to seek orders after second-half reliability evaluations, with mass production planned for 2027.\\n    Quote: According to the semiconductor industry on the 12th, LG Electronics' Production Research Institute (PRI) completed development of an AI server rack prototype matching the compute tray specifications of Nvidia's \\\"Vera Rubin\\\" in the first half of the year. LG plans to secure orders from global big tech companies after reliability evaluations in the second half and begin mass production next year.\", \"- e359 [party_statement; gurufocus.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dedacecd6d2ed5192c307199 2026-07-13] NVIDIA said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule.\\n    Quote: The company said development of its next-generation Rubin Ultra platform remains on schedule\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\", \"- e427 [third_party_view; 247wallst.com; original source 247wallst.com 2026-07-14; from gnews:ac8a489e54fbb1b85a1c7a2c 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Blackwell 300 was ramping, with the Vera Rubin platform queued behind it.\\n    Quote: Blackwell 300 is ramping, and the Vera Rubin platform is queued behind it.\", \"- e445 [party_statement; ebc.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:f83ae0a4f01c18d48f20a629 2026-07-14] NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin architecture remains on track for late-2026 delivery, according to the article.\\n    Quote: the Vera Rubin architecture remains officially on track for late 2026\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e90 (); both are in force: Reports said NVIDIA's upcoming Vera Rubin server systems were delayed; the item does not specify the extent or timing.\"]\nCONTROL 11\nRULER How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026? 2027-12-31\nJUDGED {'view_id': 'v4', 'question': 'How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?', 'looks_at': 'Calendar 2026 data-center capital expenditures by the four largest AI hyperscalers', 'due_day': '2027-03-31', 'year': '2026', 'kind': 'theme'}\nITEMS [{\"id\": \"i256\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"Nvidia Stock Is Down 17% From Its High. Is the Artificial Intelligence (AI) Leader Finally Cheap?\", \"passage\": \"This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures . Next year, Nvidia claims this group will spend more than $1 trillion.\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"big four AI hyperscalers' own plans (2026); NVIDIA's claim (2027)\", \"what\": \"data-center capital expenditure of the big four\", \"how_much\": \"around $650bn (2026); more than $1 trillion (2027)\", \"period\": \"calendar 2026; calendar 2027\", \"status\": \"plan (2026); forecast by NVIDIA (2027)\"}}, {\"id\": \"i232\", \"day\": \"2026-07-07\", \"title\": \"A Circuit Board Problem Just Delayed Nvidia's Next AI System to 2028 And Chip Stocks Are Already Feeling the Fallout\", \"passage\": \"2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion\", \"meaning\": {\"who\": \"Alphabet / Google\", \"w