ead this as the same claim as e41; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e111 [third_party_view; Allen Harris; original source Goldman Sachs ; from gnews:54aa9ce326115cedf8857512 2026-07-06] Goldman Sachs estimated that annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Goldman Sachs estimates annual AI infrastructure capital expenditures could reach $765 billion in 2026\", \"- e122 [third_party_view; the-decoder.com; original source Gary Tan of Allspring Global Investments ; from gnews:795ea94e1100415a67fd1a96 2026-07-06] Gary Tan of Allspring Global Investments said the reported Kyber delay did not necessarily mean overall AI spending would shrink.\\n    Quote: A Kyber delay doesn't necessarily mean overall AI spending will shrink, said Gary Tan of Allspring Global Investments, according to Bloomberg .\", \"- e40 [fact; fool.com; original source The four largest AI hyperscalers ; from gnews:92c7e54d38dc2916aa185568 2026-07-04] The four largest AI hyperscalers plan around $650 billion of data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: The big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e148, e152; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e80 [party_statement; fool.com analyst; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:71df54965281684cc500960f 2026-07-06] NVIDIA management forecast that hyperscaler spending would exceed $1 trillion in 2027, after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026.\\n    Quote: During its last quarterly conference call, management forecast that it expects hyperscaler spending to top $1 trillion in 2027 after reaching a projected $650 billion in 2026 .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e41, e149; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e148 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:f8191f5bb960d79e47c73d6c 2026-07-07] The author estimates that the four largest AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: This year, the big four AI hyperscalers plan to spend around $650 billion on data center capital expenditures .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e161 [party_statement; 24/7 Wall St.; original source Google ; from gnews:295fceb25273abae9bb6c995 2026-07-07] Google guided 2026 capital expenditures to $190 billion.\\n    Quote: 2026 capex is guided up tp $190 billion.\", \"- e280 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reports analysts expect NVIDIA’s share within Meta to decline while major cloud providers’ overall AI capital expenditures rise significantly.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\", \"- e152 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source fool.com (analyst) 2026-07-07; from gnews:d0f3f83296df884fae64921e 2026-07-07] The author estimates that AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: While the AI hyperscalers plan to spend $650 billion on data center capital expenditures this year, next year that figure could be over $1 trillion.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e40, e315; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e386 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Meta ; from gnews:221f52333c8f5e936e515c4d 2026-07-13] Meta raised its 2026 capital-expenditure forecast to $125–145 billion and launched Meta Compute to rent excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\\n    Quote: Meta raised 2026 capex to $125 to $145 billion, then quietly launched Meta Compute, a service renting its excess internal AI capacity to external enterprises.\", \"- e280 [third_party_view; gurufocus.com; original source gurufocus.com 2026-07-10; from gnews:4c201dc59ba0c7579bfef4db 2026-07-10] GuruFocus reports analysts expect NVIDIA’s share within Meta to decline while major cloud providers’ overall AI capital expenditures rise significantly.\\n    Quote: However, analysts remain optimistic about NVIDIA's future, suggesting that while its share within Meta may decline, overall AI capital expenditures from major cloud service providers are expected to rise significantly.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e398; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e398 [third_party_view; fool.com; original source Meta, Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon ; from gnews:84e90d3da2d3779da0e7bdb0 2026-07-14] Meta, Microsoft, Alphabet, and Amazon are planning higher capital expenditures in calendar 2026.\\n    Quote: Hyperscalers, including Meta Platforms , Microsoft , Alphabet , and Amazon , are planning higher capital expenditures in 2026.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e280; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\", \"- e412 [third_p